From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:36:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] B70-0040: routed experts split between VRAM (hot) and
 pinned host RAM (cold) for XPU W4A16 MoE

For hosts whose VRAM cannot hold every routed expert (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on 2x B70: 29 GiB of experts per
rank at EP 2). Each rank keeps the B70_MOE_HOT_EXPERTS most-routed of its local experts per layer (ranked by
B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_RANKINGS, e.g. the checkpoint's static_hot_cache_rankings.json) as the layer's ordinary
parameters; the rest live in pinned host memory, which the same XPU int4 grouped GEMM reads through a UVA view.
Both kernel calls see the full topk_ids and map only their own experts (expert_map -1 elsewhere, the mechanism
EP already uses); the outputs are summed. Bit-exact against all experts in VRAM (tests/kernels/moe).

Load path: create_weights gets the hot count; the weight loader writes cold experts into CPU twins (explicitly
on CPU: the model is built under a default-device context); after loading each layer's twins are repacked into
the kernel layout (transpose, unsigned -> signed int4) inside 1 GiB pinned chunks (torch rounds single pinned
blocks up to a power of two, ~30 % waste) and dropped.

Off by default (B70_MOE_HOTCOLD unset): nothing changes. MTP layers are never split.
B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_MEMLOG=1 logs device memory after every layer's split.

Port to 0.32 (from our 0.30 carry of Niluthon/qwen38-flash-tp2@e536e33
patches/vllm/0040, Apache-2.0):
- routed_experts.py: the hot/cold route goes after 0.32 fused-shared-expert quantizer block.
- xpu_moe.py: b70_apply_hotcold applies the 0.32 stock remap of topk_ids == -1 to a
  non-owned expert (EP > 1); -1 in both maps, so both calls skip it.
- The hot/cold XpuFusedMoe impls never take wu1ff group ownership nor the astra direct
  path (both need exactly 128 local experts), so B70_ASTRA_OWNERSHIP does not matter here;
  at TP4 the c=1 astra direct op is lost on split layers (a cost to measure).
Off by default (B70_MOE_HOTCOLD unset).
